@Calinou yes, it appears to behave as expected in the inspector window and using GDScript.

I noticed there is existing code that triggers if there is an attempt to set an offset or color at a position greater than the number of points:

```
if (points.size() <= pos) {
	points.resize(pos + 1);
	is_sorted = false;
}
```

This behaviour doesn't seem very intuitive and works unexpectedly with the "fixed" sorting technique, since the new points created each have an offset of 0. I would think it would be better to throw an error in this case as the `get_color` and `get_offset` methods already do?
